jmon is a performance monitor for FreeBSD modelled on nmon. Its interactive
screen shows CPU, memory, disks (with latency and queue depth), network, TCP,
filesystems, ZFS ARC and pools, jails, bhyve VMs, temperatures and top
processes, toggled with single keys.

The same data can be exported as OpenTelemetry metrics over OTLP (gRPC or
HTTP, optionally TLS), served to Prometheus, or recorded to nmon-compatible
files for nmon analyser. Everything is read through sysctl(3) and related
interfaces, so jmon runs unprivileged.
